    <!-- Guide Screen -->
    <string name="guide_subtitle">Camera operation guide, touch calibration gestures and troubleshooting</string>
    <string name="guide_sec1_title">1. Overview of 3 Camera Modes</string>
    <string name="guide_sec1_content">• Turn Signal Camera (LaneWatch): Blind-spot camera automatically pops up when turning left or right, and hides after a configurable delay. In hazard mode, both sides appear side-by-side.\n• ADAS BSD Radar Alert: If a vehicle or motorcycle enters your blind spot, BYD radar triggers a flashing red warning border on the PiP in real-time.\n• Digital Rearview Mirror: Toggle via steering wheel shortcut button or double-tap the window to close quickly.\n• Front Wheels (Curb Monitor): Pops up on shift out of P or when steering past the threshold angle, and automatically cuts off at higher speeds.</string>
    <string name="guide_sec2_title">2. Touch Gestures in Calibration Studio</string>
    <string name="guide_sec2_content">• 1-Finger Pan: Drag to pan and reposition the camera view.\n• 2-Finger Pinch Zoom: Pinch to zoom in for clarity or zoom out for ultra-wide angle.\n• 2-Finger Rotate: Rotate gesture for fine-tuning angle in real-time.\n• Tap [Save &amp; View]: Permanently saves camera calibration to storage.</string>
    <string name="guide_sec3_title">3. Troubleshooting</string>
    <string name="guide_sec3_content">• Window does not pop up on turn signal: Check Overlay Permission and master switch on Home tab.\n• Steering wheel button not responding: Check Accessibility Service under \'System Diagnostics\'.\n• App does not start on car power on: Open \'System Settings\' and tap [🛡️ Unblock Autostart Now] to bypass BYD DiLink background restrictions.</string>

    <!-- About Screen -->
    <string name="about_subtitle">Software specifications, engineering credits and licensing</string>
    <string name="about_edition">OEM Automotive Infotainment Edition</string>
    <string name="about_sec_arch">SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE</string>
    <string name="about_arch_desc">• Graphic Engine: OpenGL ES 2.0 Real-time Shaders\n• Inter-Process Communication: Android Binder to BYDAutoServer (autoservice)\n• Vehicle Integration: Native BYD Hardware Sensors &amp; CAN Radar Properties\n• Platform: Engineered specifically for BYD DiLink 3.0 / 4.0 / 5.0 Infotainment systems</string>
    <string name="about_sec_credits">CREDITS &amp; LICENSES</string>
    <string name="about_credits_desc">• Developed by: Galalike,NineOAD &amp; BYD Automotive Community Thailand\n• Open Source Libraries: AndroidX, Google Material Components, KaTeX, WebRTC\n• Software License: Dedicated for BYD vehicle infotainment integration without modifying vehicle safety systems.</string>

